]. These approaches can reduce trial-and-error experimentation and improve reproducibility, especially when dealing with multivariate optimization of complex systems. Establishing consensus protocols, promoting interlaboratory harmonization, and aligning method validation with international guidelines are essential to ensure reproducibility, scalability, and regulatory compliance. Only through such efforts can the full potential of microextraction techniques be realized in routine hormone determination.
